  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\nThe `DistributionCreator` contract enforces a minimum reward amount (`rewardTokenMinAmounts`) for whitelisted tokens to ensure campaigns meet a specific economic threshold. This validation is intended to prevent spam and ensure that campaigns are viable for the off-chain reward computation engine.\n\nHowever, the validation logic in `_createCampaign` checks the **gross** amount provided by the user *before* protocol fees are calculated and deducted.\n\nhttps://github.com/code-423n4/2025-11-merkl/blob/main/contracts/DistributionCreator.sol#L533\n```solidity\n// if the amount distributed is too small with respect to what is allowed\nif ((newCampaign.amount * HOUR) / newCampaign.duration < rewardTokenMinAmount) revert Errors.CampaignRewardTooLow();\n```\n\nImmediately after this check passes, the contract calculates the fees and updates the campaign amount to the **net** value:\n\nhttps://github.com/code-423n4/2025-11-merkl/blob/main/contracts/DistributionCreator.sol#L535-L538\n```solidity\n// Computing fees and pulling tokens\nuint256 campaignAmountMinusFees = _computeFees(newCampaign.campaignType, newCampaign.amount);\n// ...\nnewCampaign.amount = campaignAmountMinusFees;\n```\n\nIf a user creates a campaign with an amount exactly equal to (or slightly above) the minimum, the subsequent fee deduction will drop the final distributed amount **below** the mandatory threshold.\n\n**Impact:**\nThis discrepancy allows for the creation of \"Zombie Campaigns\"—campaigns that are valid on-chain but violate the protocol's minimum economic constraints off-chain.\n1.  **Fund Lock:** The campaign is successfully created, and the net funds are transferred to the `Distributor` contract.\n2.  **Service Denial:** The Merkl off-chain engine, which reads chain state to compute rewards, enforces the `rewardTokenMinAmount` logic to filter out spam or dust campaigns. Because the stored campaign amount is now below this threshold, the engine will likely ignore or reject the campaign.\n3.  **Loss of Assets:** Since the engine ignores the campaign, no Merkle root updates will be generated for it. The user's funds remain stuck in the `Distributor` contract indefinitely, indistinguishable from other idle funds, unless manual governance intervention occurs.\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nUpdate `_createCampaign` to validate the **net** amount (after fees) against the minimum threshold. This ensures that only campaigns capable of distributing the required minimum rewards are accepted.\n\n```diff\n    function _createCampaign(CampaignParameters memory newCampaign) internal returns (bytes32) {\n        uint256 rewardTokenMinAmount = rewardTokenMinAmounts[newCampaign.rewardToken];\n        // ... (duration check) ...\n        if (rewardTokenMinAmount == 0) revert Errors.CampaignRewardTokenNotWhitelisted();\n\n-       if ((newCampaign.amount * HOUR) / newCampaign.duration < rewardTokenMinAmount) revert Errors.CampaignRewardTooLow();\n        \n        // Computing fees and pulling tokens\n        uint256 campaignAmountMinusFees = _computeFees(newCampaign.campaignType, newCampaign.amount);\n        \n+       // Validate NET amount\n+       if ((campaignAmountMinusFees * HOUR) / newCampaign.duration < rewardTokenMinAmount) revert Errors.CampaignRewardTooLow();\n\n        if (newCampaign.creator == address(0)) newCampaign.creator = msg.sender;\n        _pullTokens(newCampaign.creator, newCampaign.rewardToken, newCampaign.amount, campaignAmountMinusFees);\n        newCampaign.amount = campaignAmountMinusFees;\n        // ...\n```",
  "proof_of_concept": "### Proof of Concept (PoC)\n\nCopy and paste the following code into `test/c4/C4PoC.t.sol`. This test demonstrates a campaign being created where the final amount stored (`90e18`) is less than the minimum required amount (`100e18`), and verifies the funds are transferred to the Distributor.\n\n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: UNLICENSED\npragma solidity ^0.8.17;\n\nimport { Fixture } from \"../Fixture.t.sol\";\nimport { CampaignParameters } from \"../../contracts/struct/CampaignParameters.sol\";\n\ncontract C4PoC is Fixture {\n    function setUp() public override {\n        super.setUp();\n\n        // 1. Set Protocol Fees to 10%\n        vm.prank(governor);\n        creator.setFees(1e8); \n\n        // 2. Set Minimum Amount for Angle Token to 100 tokens\n        // This ensures the off-chain engine only processes campaigns with significant value\n        vm.startPrank(guardian);\n        address[] memory tokens = new address[](1);\n        uint256[] memory amounts = new uint256[](1);\n        tokens[0] = address(angle);\n        amounts[0] = 100e18; \n        creator.setRewardTokenMinAmounts(tokens, amounts);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        // Fund Alice\n        angle.mint(address(alice), 1000e18);\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        angle.approve(address(creator), type(uint256).max);\n    }\n\n    function test_submissionValidity() external {\n        // Alice creates a campaign with exactly 100 tokens (the min required)\n        // Fees are 10%, so net amount will be 90.\n        uint256 amount = 100e18;\n        \n        CampaignParameters memory params = CampaignParameters({\n            campaignId: bytes32(0),\n            creator: address(alice),\n            rewardToken: address(angle),\n            amount: amount, \n            campaignType: 0,\n            startTimestamp: uint32(block.timestamp + 100),\n            duration: 3600,\n            campaignData: \"\"\n        });\n\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        bytes32 campaignId = creator.createCampaign(params);\n\n        CampaignParameters memory created = creator.campaign(campaignId);\n\n        // 1. Verify net amount is 90 (100 - 10% fee)\n        assertEq(created.amount, 90e18, \"Net amount should be 90\");\n        \n        // 2. Verify we bypassed the minimum check\n        // The campaign exists with 90 tokens, even though min is 100.\n        // This confirms the creation of a \"Zombie Campaign\".\n        assertTrue(created.amount < 100e18, \"Campaign created below min threshold\");\n\n        // 3. Verify funds are locked in distributor\n        // The funds move to the distributor, but the campaign is invalid off-chain.\n        address distributorAddr = creator.distributor();\n        assertEq(angle.balanceOf(distributorAddr), 90e18, \"Funds trapped in Distributor\");\n    }\n}\n```",
